MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_001: Goliath! Ahem. Do you have a moment? There's\na matter I'd like to discuss.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_002: I've long waited to have a proper chat with you.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_003: Me? What did you wanna talk to me for?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_004: Of course, there's no way you would recall.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_005: But before I began serving at Kalla's temple—\nwhen I was still living at home...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_006: my parents took me out sightseeing in Dagsion on my\ntwelfth birthday.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_007: And I saw a match of yours. So stirring! So moving!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_008: Wow! You remember a fight I was in all that\ntime ago?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_009: I probably couldn't tell ya much about it. Been in a\nlotta matches over the years.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_010: Is that so? I remember it so vividly, for my part!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_011: Even with your arms bound in chains, you never\ngave in. The heroic image you cast!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_012: Chains? That would've been... Oh.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_013: You saw the exhibition match I was in that only\nnobles were invited to watch.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_014: Yes! Exactly right. So you do remember!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_015: Mustering all your strength, you burst out of your\nshackles, and the chains let fly. The sight of it!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_016: Hrmph...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_017: Oh dear! Goliath. Are you in pain?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_018: If that's what you want to talk about, I'm thinkin'\nlet's not.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_019: But I had more to say!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_020: Stop—just forget about it, OK? I ain't listening.\nSee you around.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_021: Oh dear. I was hoping, at last, we could discuss it...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_C_022: Hurts thinkin' about that one. Damn. I thought\nI was over it.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_001: Goliath? Goliath! Please wait.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_002: I was hoping we might at last discuss the\nexhibition match.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_003: I got nothing to say. I told you to forget about that.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_004: Indeed, I recall very well. However, I simply can't\nforget it.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_005: I must talk to you about that day, and, no, I will\nnot relent!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_006: Ugh, alright, say what you gotta say. Quick-like.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_007: Alright! I just wanted to tell you how grateful I am.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_008: You see, if not for that match, I would not be the\nperson I am today.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_009: Huh? What do you mean?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_010: I used to be stricken with the most severe timidness.\nI was attuned at all times to my parents' reactions.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_011: Even on my own birthday, I caved to their\ninsistence that we holiday in Dagsion.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_012: But you're not timid. And you don't just go along\nwith things.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_013: Indeed not! Not since that match.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_014: The moment you snapped the chains and roared,\na fiery thrill erupted in my chest!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_015: Embarrassing as it is to say, I was so moved that I\nbegan to stand up and cheer.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_016: It was the first time in my life I had ever raised\nmy voice.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_017: I don't enjoy bloodshed per se, but the sight of you\nthat day is burned into my memory.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_018: I keep the proof of that with me. Look.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_019: Uh— Whoa.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_020: The chains you snapped. They flew into the\nspectator seats.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_021: My parents, they were utterly panicked, but for\nmy part—it was the best birthday gift I'd ever gotten.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_022: I thought you were makin' fun of me, bringing up\nthe match.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_023: No, of course not! After all your amazing\nachievements?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_024: Yeah—gettin' shackled up, just to make the\nwell-to-do happy. Amazing, right?!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_025: Oh, the chains! They're shattered...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_026: Uh...sorry. I didn't mean to do that.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_027: No, it's— It's immaterial. I was able to express my\ngratitude.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_028: I'll try to let go of that day. Now, if you'll excuse me...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_B_029: Goliath, stupid. You made her cry! So she's the girl...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_001: *sigh*
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_002: Hey, lady. Got a minute? I wanna talk about the\nfight you saw me in.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_003: Of course. Let's find somewhere quiet to talk.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_004: So, that match. Sounds like it's a day you really like\nremembering, and I don't fault you.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_005: But it's a day I hate thinking about. The worst match\nof my life.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_006: Because you were made a spectacle by the nobles?
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_007: Well...I agreed to it. The nobles being there meant I\nwas in for a big payday.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_008: And I had a buddy, he—he was really sick, and the\ndoctor was expensive. I wanted to help pay his bills.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_009: But then I got in the match, and the chains were\ndigging into my skin, and I got so mad...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_010: I snapped them and threw 'em into the stands.\n"Take that!" I said.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_011: You mean those chains were...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_012: The crowd kept screaming at me—I just couldn't\ntake it anymore.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_013: Afterward, they told me because of the harm I\ncaused to a noble, I wasn't getting one coin.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_014: No! But— But I was fine!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_015: They didn't care. Took the prize money and spent it\non a big party for the nobles.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_016: Wanted to cheer them up after what happened,\nI guess. And my friend, he died.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_017: Oh...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_018: I got tied up and shouted at, then got so mad I\ncaused my friend's death. It... Yeah, it sucked.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_019: But I'm glad you were OK.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_020: You really could've been hurt. Sorry.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_021: Do not apologize! I should apologize!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_022: I had no knowledge of the anger and pain you\nwere feeling...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_023: Goliath, you've told me so much about yourself, and\nI'll respond in kind.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_024: No matter how hard times were, when I held those\nchains tight, I felt courage. A fighting spirit!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_025: Thusly did I keep striving ever and ever forward,\nuntil I blossomed into the Blue Rose of Caelus!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_026: Huh...
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_027: The girl you nearly killed has grown into a\nflourishing flower. So you take THAT!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_028: Heh, still smilin' at me after what I almost did\nto you. You got guts!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_029: OK, I'm good on feelings talk. You wanna play me\nsomething? Whatever tune you like!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_030: With pleasure! Tonight I shall regale you for as long\nas you like.
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_031: Consider this a return gift for the birthday present\nyou gave me that day. Long overdue, I say!
MID_SE_Gol_Oly_A_032: Wow... I can really feel your emotions and stuff!